{
  "description": "Recorded ARC POST /v1/tx answers with an HTTP 2xx code and the verdict a broadcaster must give on each. The body's txStatus decides; the HTTP code never does. Shared with the other ports (rs-sdk, py-sdk): the same bodies, the same verdicts.",
  "sources": [
    "ts-stack@edf6e03 packages/sdk/src/transaction/broadcasters/ARC.ts:16-22 (the failure set), 28-38 (the accepted set), 110-180 (the verdict on a 2xx)",
    "go-sdk@511b58c transaction/broadcaster/arc.go:185-301 (the Go port's reading of the same rule)",
    "arc@e7efc5b internal/api/handler/default.go:489-500 (the shape of the 2xx body), pkg/api/arc.go:429 (competingTxs is a nullable array), internal/metamorph/metamorph_api/metamorph_api.proto:13-28 (the status words ARC emits)",
    "bsv-stack-lean issue #35, P0-2; corpus/scenarios/2026-10-08-p0-2-arc-2xx-rejected-is-success.md"
  ],
  "txid": "4d76b00f29e480e0a933cef9d9ffe303d6ab919e2cdb265dd2cea41089baa85a",
  "competing_txid": "f67cfb4c12b221ab1b5fef6fdb5a72f82ebc6aad8f28c6d0e5427043a2c5b0a9",
  "notes": [
    "txid is the id of the Go SDK test-vector transaction every ARC HTTP test of this crate submits (tests/broadcaster_http_tests.rs, TEST_TX_HEX).",
    "competing_txid is the display-order id of that transaction's input's source transaction, a plausible competitor; blockHash, blockHeight, merklePath and timestamp values are synthetic and never read by the verdict.",
    "expect.result is success or failure. On failure: code, description, more (null when none) and txid equal to the submitted transaction's. On success: message (the status word) and competing_txs (null when none).",
    "An explicit competingTxs: null is what ARC sends on an ordinary 2xx (pkg/api/arc.go:429 has no omitempty; doc/api.md:1512 documents [string] or null); this vector reads null as absent. The reference at the pin answers ERR_INVALID_RESPONSE for a null (ARC.ts:129-132 read a non-array that is not undefined as invalid); not run, a reading.",
    "2026-10-08, the owner's ruling (bsv-stack-lean #35): QUEUED, REQUESTED_BY_NETWORK and CONFIRMED are accepted as the reference's own spec (specs/broadcast/arc.yaml:407-415) and go-sdk accept them; the reference's TypeScript code returns an invalid response for them. An unknown word (FOOBAR) stays an invalid response."
  ],
